id: pm-beads-rzz1
title: Fail closed on combined scalar publishes and redirection-adjacent heredoc delimiters
description: "Greptile findings 3890389297 and 3890389299 identify two publish-attestation bypasses: a command with unresolved scalar publisher and subcommand can evade both fail-closed predicates, and heredoc delimiter extraction can absorb an adjacent output redirection and suppress later executable publishes."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-30T20:04:31.075Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-30T20:08:21.762Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-30T20:08:21.249Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-30T20:08:21.249Z"
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: Combined unresolved scalar publisher/subcommand forms fail closed; joined and separated heredoc delimiters stop before redirection operators; audit-level regressions include attested siblings; source-only revert proof fails; full repository gates pass
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-30T20:08:20.818Z",pi-agent,"Greptile 3890389297 reproduced: with only scripts/verify-release-publish-attestation.ts reverted, the combined $CMD $SUB attested-sibling regression changed failure counts from [1,1,1,1,1] to [1,1,1,1,0], SOURCE_ONLY_REVERT_EXIT=1. Restored source fails closed. Greptile 3890389299 did not reproduce: both cat <<EOF>out and cat << EOF>out regressions passed against the pre-finding scanner because topLevelCommands already splits > as an operator before delimiter extraction; no scanner change retained. Reacted +1/-1 respectively. npm test passed 420/420; coverage is 100% lines/branches/functions; docstring and typecheck pass."
files[3]{path,scope}:
  scripts/verify-release-publish-attestation.ts,project
  scripts/shell-command-scan.ts,project
  test/verify-release-publish-attestation.test.ts,project
